Spec: Application package

Purpose:
  The `aikana` Python package. It is organized into feature packages that follow the layering described in
  ./architecture.sdd, and it provides the entry point that composes and serves them as a FastHTML app.

Structure:
  ./__init__.py: package marker
  ./main.py: the composition root; builds the shared database connection and each feature's repository and
    service, registers every feature's routes on the FastHTML app, and binds to the `$PORT` environment variable
  ./architecture.sdd: the Clean Architecture / Ports-and-Adapters contract shared by every feature package below
  ./shared/: cross-cutting kernel (database connection, page layout shell) with no business rules of its own
  ./auth/: admin login, logout and the write guard used by other feature packages
  ./courses/: the Course entity and the per-course calendar view
  ./lessons/: the Lesson entity
  ./holidays/: the Holiday entity
  ./semester/: the semester wall planner view
  ./day_dialog/: the admin dialog for adding or editing a Lesson or a Holiday on a given day

References:
  ./architecture.sdd

Owns:
  ./__init__.py
  ./main.py

Must:
  `python -m aikana.main` starts the server on the port given by `$PORT`, defaulting to `8000`.
  Every feature package below has a same-basename spec inside it, following ./architecture.sdd.
  Views render for unauthenticated visitors without any editing affordances.

Tasks:
  [ ] Implement ./shared/, then ./auth/, then ./courses/, ./lessons/ and ./holidays/, then ./semester/ and
    ./day_dialog/, and finally wire them together in ./main.py
